{"chunk_id": "ba86fa39b496", "text": "In this episode of the Aranya Parva, Indra (disguised as a Brahmana) persists in asking Karna for his divine armor and earrings\u2014gifts he was born with that make him nearly invincible. Though Karna offers immense wealth and even a kingdom instead, the Brahmana refuses anything else. Recognizing the visitor as Indra and aware that surrendering the armor will lead to his own death, Karna still agrees, but only in exchange for a powerful celestial weapon. Indra grants him the Vasavi dart, which can kill a single mighty enemy before returning to Indra. Karna then cuts the armor and earrings from his own body and gives them away, astonishing the heavens with his resolve. Indra departs satisfied, weakening Karna for the future war, while the Pandavas rejoice and the Kauravas are dismayed.\nIndra, disguised as a Brahmana, obtains Karna\u2019s divine armor and earrings in exchange for a one\u2011use spear after Karna willingly cuts them from his own body.\nThemes: self-sacrifice, divine deception, honor and vows, fate and vulnerability, exchange of divine weapons", "vector": [0.007837445475161076, -0.02625039592385292, 0.002401689300313592, -0.008153634145855904, 0.0016271949280053377, 0.03011193498969078, -0.03700081631541252, -0.017679661512374878, -0.019294243305921555, -0.023128872737288475, 0.01975170709192753, 0.012371727265417576, 0.018621500581502914, -0.0031517967581748962, -0.012566822580993176, 0.006357412785291672, 0.04205983504652977, -0.004961472935974598, 0.03151123970746994, -0.027878431603312492, -0.0088129211217165, -0.00947220902889967, -0.005677943117916584, 0.027690064162015915, -0.01343465968966484, -0.0020720455795526505, 0.01539233885705471, -0.028282077983021736, 0.010918604210019112, -0.03013884648680687, -0.0005314662703312933, -0.007420345209538937, -0.01757202297449112, 0.005947039928287268, -0.02409762144088745, 0.005489575210958719, -0.015540341846644878, -0.025308556854724884, 0.014800325967371464, 0.